{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/406","id":4850289521,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOgxrpM8AAAABIRmLcQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/406","diff_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/406.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/406.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/issues/406","number":406,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Undo – Every edit registers through the graph that made it","user":{"login":"tobyspark","id":197773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Nzc3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/197773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark","html_url":"https://github.com/tobyspark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Genie –\r\n\r\n> Supersedes the undo half of #396 · Design reference: [PUBLISHING_AND_SETTINGS.md](link)\r\n> \r\n> 1 of 6. Each layer is final-state code: nothing here is removed by a later PR, except the temporary lines listed below.\r\n> \r\n> ### What it establishes\r\n> - Undo steps register through `Graph.registerUndo` on the graph the edit was made in, and resolve the root's undo manager when a sub graph has none of its own. `UndoRegistrationTests` fails any core code that registers on the undo manager directly.\r\n> - A step holds ids and values, and finds what it acts on by id when it runs.\r\n> - Compound edits run through `performEdit(named:)`, which keeps the edit's name through undo and redo. Single steps name their inverse pair with `nameEdit`.\r\n> - Publishing, renaming a published port, notes and parameter values set through controls are undo steps.\r\n> - `Graph.undo()` and `redo()` commit a control's change held for a pause first, so an undo never passes over it.\r\n> \r\n> ### Not in this PR\r\n> - Proxy handling and the closed `published` setter (#2).\r\n> - Settings as values and the Fabric Editor's Undo and Redo commands (#3).\r\n> - Create Subgraph keeps its embedding with suspended registration until #4, so \"nothing inside a compound edit is suppressed\" is added to AGENTS.md there.\r\n> \r\n> ### Temporary lines\r\n> - Two `registerUndo` calls in the old Create Subgraph embedding, and the `disconnect` flag on `delete(node:)`. Both go in #4.\r\n> - `registerUndo(on:)` in StrategyNode's `strategy` didSet. It goes in #3.\r\n> - One `ParameterGroupView` line. It changes in #6.","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:27:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:36:53Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"947ea6b93204f258304ecafbf991ce8b9f6dc168","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/406/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/406/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/issues/406/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/statuses/d1015950508f4f0a874f51fe702f9b2dc8fece7f","head":{"label":"Fabric-Project:stack/1-undo-foundation","ref":"stack/1-undo-foundation","sha":"d1015950508f4f0a874f51fe702f9b2dc8fece7f","user":{"